                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0ef7f676-9ddf-329d-9eaf-e3d343e91c26",
                        "entry_id": "5b7e6d8f-c737-3294-870b-9080332d6aff",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Cours des planètes et des astres, lorsque, par leur mouvement périodique, ils sont revenus au même point."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "79378eb1-95bc-4d4a-8f4d-9ef90b06defd",
                                "sense_id": "0ef7f676-9ddf-329d-9eaf-e3d343e91c26",
                                "text": "Avant que le cours de Saturne soit révolu."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b0f914cc-9762-32de-80b8-32eee1a06751",
                        "entry_id": "5b7e6d8f-c737-3294-870b-9080332d6aff",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qualifie une période de temps qui est achevée, complète."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "123c01d4-2873-4131-92a2-e52fd7d36a49",
                                "sense_id": "b0f914cc-9762-32de-80b8-32eee1a06751",
                                "text": "Le temps où l’infanterie décidait des batailles était révolu. La guerre se transformait en une question de matériel, d’entraînement et de connaissances spéciales très compliquées."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1b7b7a3c-5dda-4999-b386-7fc96cd32c9e",
                                "sense_id": "b0f914cc-9762-32de-80b8-32eee1a06751",
                                "text": "Moi, ce qui m’intéressait, c’était jeudi prochain, et les racontars de M. Michel sur des époques révolues, qui avaient consommé leurs calendriers, ne m’intéressaient pas plus qu’une promenade dans un cimetière."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8aebf5e1-5989-49b0-88a0-28e3cb9e3314",
                                "sense_id": "b0f914cc-9762-32de-80b8-32eee1a06751",
                                "text": "Seul témoin de cette époque révolue où la forge de Vendresse sortait 3 tonnes de fonte par jour, rugissant jour et nuit, où la sidérurgie ardennaise battait son plein, son haut-fourneau est d'ailleurs un lieu incontournable."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4be3c8ee-7327-43c2-9990-1d7727bb1520",
                                "sense_id": "b0f914cc-9762-32de-80b8-32eee1a06751",
                                "text": "Je dessine un carré avec des phrases compactes : c’est la maison. À l’intérieur un passé révolu séjourne, des présences vagues laissant des objets sur les meubles : un fragment de cristal brisé, une poignée de terre. Les murs connaissent l’histoire, ils l’inspirent, ils l’expirent. Elle fait partie de la charpente."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2cc074bd-f042-4ee4-8a53-0886fb4503f8",
                        "source_entry_id": "5b7e6d8f-c737-3294-870b-9080332d6aff",
                        "source_sense_id": "b0f914cc-9762-32de-80b8-32eee1a06751",
                        "source_sense_description": "Qualifie une période de temps qui est achevée, complète.",
                        "target_lang_word": "bygone",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bygone",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7903184f-ef7c-39e6-b84a-15d6ab85407f",
                                        "entry_id": "361598de-b526-3e9a-b0a7-bcbd703c53d5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having been or happened in the distant past."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98887a3c-46d5-415e-b7b5-aad35c22236e",
                                                "sense_id": "7903184f-ef7c-39e6-b84a-15d6ab85407f",
                                                "text": "I had thought (Sir) to haue held my peace, vntill\nYou had drawne Oathes from him, not to ſtay: you (Sir)\nCharge him too coldly. Tell him, you are ſure\nAll in Bohemias well: this ſatisfaction,\nThe ''by-gone-day proclaym'd, ſay this to him,\nHe's beat from his beſt ward."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c044aa58-76e2-44a3-b81e-c3f6ccd6cbba",
                                                "sense_id": "7903184f-ef7c-39e6-b84a-15d6ab85407f",
                                                "text": "Near by he could see the thicket of raspberry canes, growing tall and close like a tropical jungle, in whose shadow he had played with the Boy on bygone mornings."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "475ee747-ab62-4850-a7ec-458905fdff37",
                                                "sense_id": "7903184f-ef7c-39e6-b84a-15d6ab85407f",
                                                "text": "Travellers over the London & North Western main line in bygone days will need no reminder of the pattering of cinders on the carriage roofs, the fountains of sparks from the chimneys at night and the distance from which the exhaust of approaching locomotives could be heard, due to the fierceness of their blast in such conditions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "954ee95a-99a9-475f-a818-72a9d09b0f3f",
                                                "sense_id": "7903184f-ef7c-39e6-b84a-15d6ab85407f",
                                                "text": "The modern, glass-fronted buildings surrounding the massive skyscraper Taipei 101 in the Xinyi District suggest a shift toward cleaner, starker development, but a trip to older parts of the city reveals hidden corners untouched by modernity.\nThe oldest section, Wanhua, with its winding corridors and quiet decay, offers a glimpse of the city’s bygone days. At its bustling heart is the busy Longshan Temple. I bump past a flurry of tourists, worshipers and monks selling prayer beads outside the gates to reach the controlled chaos within, where hundreds of faithful light incense and present offerings at myriad shrines to Buddha and other deities."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "bygone",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1157acaf-36f6-3583-b736-484fd33a3960",
                                        "entry_id": "1f0bbe2a-c609-33a1-a076-c4d254a54cb1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An event that happened in the past."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "plural-normally"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eff3d0eb-4923-4a0f-a15a-e177b80f03a7",
                                                "sense_id": "1157acaf-36f6-3583-b736-484fd33a3960",
                                                "text": "Jennie Fox watched it with thoughtful pleasure, and the rest were chatting and telling of bygones, enjoying a glass of egg-hot; it being a custom for them to partake of this beverage on this particular night."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "faa0bb59-bb3f-3ff6-b932-551e5a27039f",
                                        "entry_id": "1f0bbe2a-c609-33a1-a076-c4d254a54cb1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An object from the past; a relic, antique, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "plural-normally"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "696b95a6-27f5-44de-8f19-5efab9853c57",
                                                "sense_id": "faa0bb59-bb3f-3ff6-b932-551e5a27039f",
                                                "text": "And now just as the Victorians collected the minute objects with which to fill these houses, so today grown-ups are paying large sums for these bygones, while the children are given more modern houses to play with."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
